 don't have  a specific figure  i cannot sleep it will always be in my  mind trying to think about okay how do i  get this you know where can i go it's  always this little nagging doubt that  that keeps me awake at night most of it  is action figures are from a six inch  scale and most of my figures are from  from the dc sarah is either mattel or dc  direct  then for marvel is either  hasbro or marvel select  [Music]  currently i have a supplier  like a personal friend of mine right  here's the one that gonna get all this  action fitness so shout out to marvin  fool that gets all of my items from me  it's not so much a collection then it's  an obsession to me it's almost like a  drug every time i get a certain  item that has been hard to find i feel  this whole sense of  accomplishment  in the past there are certain figures  that because the way the company is sort  of distributed right there will be rare  figures that are so hard to find that  even though you search all around you  cannot find it and i was lucky enough  that  back then my work allowed me to travel  every time i travel i would visit all  the toy stores and find the figures that  singapore don't have  currently i have everything i need to  have for for marvel legends i have every  single figure produced back when it was  under toy biz in the late 90s and he  moved over to hasbro legends so i have  every single figure even the the  exclusive the variants while  during that period some of them were  really hard to get because i think  one of the ways was exclusive to like a  retailer in us that was really hard to  get even within the region you cannot  find  and this is back before the internet  days back before amazon that wave would  be the giant manual  you really got to  search high and low to find it which  eventually i managed to find i had to  pay a bit depending on prices at least  three to four times what would have gone  at retail  so the thing about collecting is uh how  you display them right collectors are  also hoarders right the only difference  between hoarders and collectors are that  the collectors are able to display them  in a very nice way and identify where  everything lies specifically  most of the items has a very special  emotional connection and memory attached  to it if you  point out to a specific figure right i  can probably tell you a bit more about  where i was what i was doing when i  purchased it to me story is also very  important it has to be  correct to that character's storyline if  you know the history of ghost rider  right so ghost rider rides a motorcycle  and because of his supernatural  abilities his motorcycle can go up  vertical surfaces power display the  ghost rider figures are all on vertical  sections spider-man is the easiest  because spider-man swings from building  the building so again if you look at all  the stuff you'll see  all the various spidermans  [Music]  swinging from location to location and i  also try not to duplicate my spider-man  in terms of the poses so every  spider-man has a unique pose that is  identifiable to his actions  [Music]  todd mcfarlane had a very unique  distinct style and whenever he drew  spider-man's web i don't throw anything  so i still have all the original  twisting ties it grew to a point where  he started to get out of hand and i  realized hey if i actually joined all  the twisty ties it looked almost  identical to top my talent swept  i had a really good friend back then he  was like a diy carpenter  he came in he suggested hey you know why  don't you put it on the ceiling you can  actually build like a walkway a catwalks  across  then i have all these walkways for  additional  collection and additional display  what i've learned is careful planning  and make sure that every figure can  stand on its own  so that when the figures are displayed  all by itself  it looks natural  i tend to arrange them by grouping again  it's always about the story so  if if like like we look 